      "card_ids": ["C29"],
      "claim": "Chloramphenicol palmitate, a long-chain ester prodrug, is almost completely bioavailable in children, showing that some long-chain esters can be well absorbed.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C30"],
      "claim": "Valomaciclovir stearate, a long-chain fatty acid ester prodrug, has >60% oral bioavailability in humans, providing another example of a well-absorbed lipophilic ester.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is orlistat, a beta-lactone GI lipase inhibitor designed for local action with negligible systemic absorption. Although some lipophilic esters show ≥20% bioavailability, the recognized non-absorbed behavior of orlistat and the only sub-threshold ester analog support F <20%.",
